 Luo, Rongrong Ji\n\n    * Published: 18 Sept 2025, Last Modified: 21 Apr 2026\n    * NeurIPS 2025 poster\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### Exploiting Instance-level Relationships in Weakly Supervised Text-to-Video Retrieval\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenReview (https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Liang_Ding3)\nciteturn2158search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.3 years ago;   * #### Retrieval-Augmented Perception: High-resolution Image Perception Meets Visual RAG\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### The Energy Loss Phenomenon in RLHF: A New Perspective on Mitigating Reward Hacking\n\nYuchun Miao, Sen Zhang, Liang Ding, Yuqi Zhang, Lefei Zhang, Dacheng Tao\n\n    * Published: 01 May 2025, Last Modified: 18 Jun 2025\n    * ICML 2025 poster\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### Retrieval-Augmented Perception: High-resolution Image Perception Meets Visual RAG\n\nWenbin Wang, Yongcheng Jing, Liang Ding, Yingjie Wang, Li Shen, Yong Luo, Bo Du, Dacheng Tao\n\n    * Published: 01 May 2025, Last Modified: 18 Jun 2025\n    * ICML 2025 oral\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### Self-Evolution Knowledge Distillation for LLM-based Machine Translation\n\nYuncheng Song, Liang Ding, Changtong Zan, Shujian Huang\n\n    * Published: 19 Dec 2024, Last Modified: 23 Dec 2024\n    * COLING 2025\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\nView all 172 publications\n\n#### Co-Authors\n\n  * Andrew Yates\n  * Ang Li\n  * Baopu Qiu\n  * Baosheng Yu\n  * Bing Wang\n  * Bo Du\n  * Boan Liu\n  * Bohao Zhou\n  * Bohua Cai\n  * Chang Li\n  * Changjian Wang\n  * Changtong Zan\n  * Changxing Ding\n  * Chao Xue\n  * Chaoyue Wang\n  * Chen Gong\n  * Chenbo Jiang\n  * Chiaming Hsu\n  * Chong Zhang\n  * Chris Biemann\n  * Chuang Liu\n  * Chunyan Miao\n  * Dacheng Tao\n  * Daize Dong\n  * Danilo P. Mandic\nView all 195 co-authors--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRethinking Legal Retrieval as Generative Article Identifier Prediction | OpenReview (https://openreview.net/forum?id=SJcpGTx0Ag)\nciteturn2158search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Research Area Keywords: retrieval for RAG\n## Rethinking Legal Retrieval as Generative Article Identifier Prediction\n\n### ACL ARR 2026 May Submission15161 Authors\n\n26 May 2026 (modified: 16 Jun 2026)ACL ARR 2026 May Submission EveryoneRevisionsBibTeXCC BY 4.0\n\nKeywords: Legal Retrieval, Information Retrieval, Self-Supervised Learning\n\nAbstract: Legal article retrieval requires mapping concrete factual disputes to abstract statutory norms, not merely matching semantically similar texts. This fact-to-norm gap makes lexical or embedding-based retrieval unreliable. We propose a simple alternative: generative statutory article identifier prediction. Given a legal question, we use a large language model (LLM) to predict canonical article identifiers, such as \\emph{Civil Code Article 243}, by leveraging its parametric legal memory and reasoning ability. The predicted identifiers are then bound to authoritative statutory texts as retrieval results. Moreover, we introduce a self-supervised statute knowledge injection strategy that teaches LLMs to associate statutes with their identifiers, without annotated query-document pairs or positive-negative samples required by common embedding-based retriever training. Experiments show that LLMs are strong zero-shot generative retrievers for legal articles, and that knowledge injection further improves recall and ranking quality.\n\nPaper Type: Short\n\nResearch Area: Information Retrieval and Text Mining\n\nResearch Area Keywords: retrieval for RAG\n\nContribution Types: NLP engineering experiment\n\nLanguages Studied: Chinese\n\nEMNLP 2026 AI Reviewing Experiment: yes\n\nSubmission Number: 15161\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC-3PO: Compact Plug-and-Play Proxy Optimization to Achieve Human-like Retrieval-Augmented Generation | OpenReview (https://openreview.net/forum?id=vfd3qMgpmW)\nciteturn2158search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 1.2 years ago; Abstract: Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems face a fundamental challenge in aligning independently developed retrievers and large language models (LLMs).\n## C-3PO: Compact Plug-and-Play Proxy Optimization to Achieve Human-like Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\n### Guoxin Chen, Minpeng Liao, Peiying Yu, Dingmin Wang, Zile Qiao, Chao Yang, Xin Zhao, Kai Fan\n\nPublished: 01 Jan 2025, Last Modified: 20 May 2025 CoRR 2025 EveryoneRevisionsBibTeXCC BY-SA 4.0\n\nAbstract: Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems face a fundamental challenge in aligning independently developed retrievers and large language models (LLMs). Existing approaches typically involve modifying either component or introducing simple intermediate modules, resulting in practical limitations and sub-optimal performance. Inspired by human search behavior -- typically involving a back-and-forth process of proposing search queries and reviewing documents, we propose C-3PO, a proxy-centric framework that facilitates communication between retrievers and LLMs through a lightweight multi-agent system. Our framework implements three specialized agents that collaboratively optimize the entire RAG pipeline without altering the retriever and LLMs. These agents work together to assess the need for retrieval, generate effective queries, and select information suitable for the LLMs. To enable effective multi-agent coordination, we develop a tree-structured rollout approach for reward credit assignment in reinforcement learning. Extensive experiments in both in-domain and out-of-distribution scenarios demonstrate that C-3PO significantly enhances RAG performance while maintaining plug-and-play flexibility and superior generalization capabilities.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJiaxin Mao | OpenReview (https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Jiaxin_Mao1)\nciteturn2158search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; RAG\n    * OpenReview Archive Direct Upload\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### SIGIR 2019 Tutorial on Explainable Recommendation and Search\n\nYi Zhang, Jiaxin Mao, Qingyao Ai, Yongfeng Zhang\n\n    * Published: 18 Jul 2019, Last Modified: 16 Jan 2026\n    * ACM\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### JADE: Bridging the Strategic-Operational Gap in Dynamic Agentic RAG\n\nYiqun Chen, Erhan Zhang, Tianyi Hu, Shijie Wang, Zixuan Yang, Meizhi Zhong, Xiaochi Wei, Yan Gao, Yi Wu, Yao Hu, Jiaxin Mao\n\n    * Published: 30 Apr 2026, Last Modified: 24 Jun 2026\n    * ICML 2026 regular\n    * Readers: Everyone\n\n  * #### E2Rank: Your Text Embedding can Also be an Effective and Efficient Listwise Reranker\n\nQi Liu, Yanzhao Zhang, Mingxin Li, Dingkun Long, Pengjun Xie, Jiaxin Mao\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2158view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn2155view0\",\"id\":8}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2158view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn2155view0\",\"id\":9}); Total lines: 1\n"
